      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea of \"deserved consequence\" is a deeply ingrained, yet ultimately flawed, concept when applied to systemic injustice. While retribution offers a satisfying narrative of punishment, it mistakes vengeance for justice, which is a moral failure in itself. True accountability, in a modern context, means addressing the root causes of harm, not just inflicting pain on the individual. Therefore, the focus on repairing the societal breach through restorative means is the only truly moral path forward.",
      "source": "target",
